--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why two licenses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

MIT is a software license; its language ("this software") reads awkwardly
when applied to an essay about Scaffold placement. CC BY is built for
documents but is a poor fit for source code. Using each where it belongs
is more correct than stretching one to cover both.
